{% comment %}
  Step 3 (shown as "Step 2 of 5") — doctor selection. Now reached from the
  new Concern Select step, not directly from Entry — see that step's own
  comment for why.

  BACKEND INTEGRATION BUILT, CURRENTLY DISCONNECTED: kal-booking-flow.js
  has a working loadDoctorsForFacility() that calls
  GET /api/public/doctors?facility_id= and matches results against
  sections/kal-doctor-cards.liquid's blocks by doctor_id (see that
  function's own comment for the full design — the doctor_id-join
  approach that lets rich card content stay Shopify-editable without new
  CMS schema work). It's just not being called right now — the backend
  branch (`preetham` in the CMS repo) exists but isn't deployed anywhere
  yet, so there's nothing for it to fetch from. The call site is
  commented out in goToStep() in kal-booking-flow.js; search for
  "loadDoctorsForFacility()" there to re-enable once that's deployed.

  Until then, this list is back to the static mockup card it had before
  that integration work (Dr. Neethu Jayachandran, hardcoded values) —
  see kal-booking-flow-doctor-card.liquid's own comment for why a mockup
  intentionally shows content no version of the real API provides.

  Single shared markup, not a __mobile + __desktop split — see the "SHARED
  STEP SHELL" comment in kal-booking-flow.css for why and how the layout
  switches at 750px.

  DESKTOP REDESIGN: this step now reuses Concern Select's own desktop
  left column ("Consultation Booking" heading, Selected Clinic, Your
  Progress stepper) and full-width footer (Need assistance + Back/
  Continue) rather than the old plain .kal-step-entry__info reuse most
  other steps still have — per the reference export, this step's left
  column looks IDENTICAL to Concern Select's, just with "Health
  concerns" now showing completed (checkmark) and "Mode & doctor" as the
  current step instead. See kal-booking-flow-step-progress.liquid (the
  stepper, parameterized by current_step) and kal-booking-flow.css's
  .kal-step-shell--progress-panel section (generalized from Concern
  Select's original build once this step needed the exact same layout)
  for how this is shared instead of duplicated. Mobile is untouched —
  still its own "Who would you like to see?" composition below, unaware
  any of this exists (.kal-step-shell__info stays display:none there).
{% endcomment %}

<div class="kal-step-doctor-select kal-step-shell kal-step-shell--progress-panel">

  <div class="kal-step-entry__info kal-step-shell__info kal-concern-select__info">
    <div class="kal-concern-select__info-scroll">
      <div class="kal-concern-select__info-header">
        <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading kal-concern-select__heading">Consultation Booking</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-concern-select__info-section">
        <p class="kal-concern-select__info-label">Selected Clinic</p>
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-facility-picker', step_number: 2, location_text: 'Indiranagar', extra_class: 'kal-concern-select__info-pill' -%}
      </div>

      {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-step-progress', current_step: 2 -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kal-step-shell__panel">

    {%- comment -%}
      Per the updated Figma spec (node 544:3781), Doctor Select's header
      is the exact same composition Concern Select uses — back button,
      mobile facility badge / desktop progress dots, close button, plus a
      mobile step progress bar underneath. Shared via the same snippet
      rather than duplicating that markup here (see
      kal-booking-flow-step-header.liquid); the old dots-only header
      (with its own inline "2/5" text and no facility badge/step-bar) is
      gone.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-step-header', back_target: 'concern-select', step_number: 2, step_total: 5, next_label: 'Date & Time', location_switchable: true -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Heading + mode toggle moved OUTSIDE .kal-step-shell__scroll (still
      siblings within .kal-step-shell__panel) per explicit instruction —
      only the doctor list itself should scroll, with these two staying
      fixed right below the progress bar, same treatment as Concern
      Select's own heading/banner. Desktop already scrolled just
      .kal-step-doctor-select__list on its own (see that class's own
      750px+ rule below) rather than this whole wrapper — this brings
      mobile in line with that, rather than changing desktop's behavior.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__intro">
      <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Choose your doctor</h2>
      <p class="kal-step-doctor-select__subtext">Select a doctor and how you&rsquo;d like to consult</p>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-toggle-group">
      <button type="button" class="kal-toggle-btn kal-toggle-btn--active" data-kal-mode="in-clinic">
        <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--location">
          {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'mode-location' -%}
        </span>
        In-Clinic
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="kal-toggle-btn" data-kal-mode="video">
        <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--video">
          {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'mode-online' -%}
        </span>
        Video Consult
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__scroll">
      {%- comment -%}
        In-Clinic mode shows only the doctor(s) whose mock home facility
        (kal-booking-flow.js's MOCK_DOCTOR_HOME_FACILITY — the same map
        the facility-switch warning uses) matches the currently selected
        facility, pre-selecting the one match; Video Consult shows all
        three with none pre-selected. renderMockDoctorsForCurrentState()
        drives this by hiding/showing and (de)selecting these same static
        cards — it doesn't fetch or clone anything. This empty state
        covers facilities with no assigned mock doctor (HSR layout,
        Jayanagar, Sarjapur).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Real Shopify data now, via the "Doctor" metaobject (Settings >
        Custom data > Metaobject definitions) instead of the 3 hardcoded
        mock cards this used to render — see that definition's fields
        (name/qualification/languages/experience/specialties/photo/
        next_slot/price) for what each entry needs. languages/specialties
        are List fields, joined here into the same pre-formatted strings
        kal-booking-flow-doctor-card.liquid already expected from the old
        hardcoded calls. First entry pre-selected (forloop.first), same
        default-selection behavior the old first hardcoded card had — no
        real facility-matching logic here yet (see this file's own
        BACKEND INTEGRATION comment above), so every entry currently shows
        regardless of the selected clinic/mode.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign placeholder_photo_url = 'kal-doctor-photo-placeholder.jpg' | asset_url -%}
      <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__list" data-kal-doctor-list>
        <p class="kal-step-doctor-select__list-empty" data-kal-doctor-list-empty hidden>
          No in-clinic doctors available at this clinic yet — try Video Consult, or switch clinics.
        </p>
        {%- for doctor in shop.metaobjects.doctor.values -%}
          {%- assign languages_joined = doctor.languages.value | join: ' &middot; ' -%}
          {%- assign tags_joined = doctor.specialties.value | join: ',' -%}
          {%- if doctor.photo.value != blank -%}
            {%- assign doctor_photo_url = doctor.photo.value | image_url: width: 200 -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- assign doctor_photo_url = placeholder_photo_url -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-doctor-card',
            name: doctor.name.value,
            degree: doctor.qualification.value,
            languages: languages_joined,
            experience: doctor.experience.value,
            tags: tags_joined,
            next_slot: doctor.next_slot.value,
            price: doctor.price.value,
            selected: forloop.first,
            photo_url: doctor_photo_url
          -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      data-kal-doctor-continue, disabled by default — Video Consult
      intentionally pre-selects no doctor (see this list's own comment),
      so a plain always-clickable data-kal-goto would let the visitor
      through with none picked. updateDoctorSelectContinueButton() in
      kal-booking-flow.js keeps this in sync with whether a card is
      currently selected, re-checked on every card click and every
      facility/mode re-render.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="kal-step-shell__footer kal-concern-select__footer kal-concern-select__footer--mobile">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-goto="slot-picker" data-kal-doctor-continue disabled>
        Continue
      </button>
    </div>

  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Desktop-only full-width footer bar — same composition as Concern
    Select's own (help text + Back/Continue split across the shared
    300px/1fr grid columns, see kal-booking-flow.css's
    .kal-step-shell--progress-panel section), a separate instance rather
    than a relocation of the mobile footer above for the same reason
    Concern Select's is (CSS can't move one element into two different
    parents across breakpoints).

    Unlike Concern Select's Back/Continue, there's no data-kal-concern-footer/
    hidden toggle here — Doctor Select's Continue was always just
    disabled (not the whole row hidden) via data-kal-doctor-continue,
    kept as-is; Back is always clickable, going to Concern Select.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-step-shell__footer kal-concern-select__footer kal-concern-select__footer--desktop">
    <div class="kal-concern-select__footer-help kal-step-entry__help">
      <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--help">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'help-circle' -%}
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-entry__help-text">Need assistance? Call us at +91 804012 3456</span>
    </div>
    <div class="kal-concern-select__footer-actions">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__back kal-concern-select__footer-back" data-kal-back="concern-select" aria-label="Back">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-left' -%}
        <span>Back</span>
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-goto="slot-picker" data-kal-doctor-continue disabled>
        Continue
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
